# Nothing in this repository redistributes a game that is still under copyright.
#
# Three kinds of file are therefore never committed:
#
#   original/    the game exactly as it shipped
#   recovered/   a reconstruction that assembles or compiles to a byte-identical
#                copy of it — legally the same thing as the binary, just in
#                source form, and easy to forget for exactly that reason
#   reference/   anything *derived* from the game: extracted sprites, memory
#                dumps, screenshots, disk images. A sprite sheet pulled out of
#                a copyrighted game is still that game, and this is the rule
#                people forget, because a PNG does not feel like a binary
#
# Every game folder follows this convention, so the rule is one pattern each.
# Everything else — the documentation, the port, our own tools — is our own work
# and is committed normally.
#
# Each game's README explains how to regenerate what is missing from a copy of
# the game you already own.

*/original/
*/recovered/
*/reference/

# Belt and braces: never commit a game binary, an archive of one, or a disk
# image, from anywhere in the tree.
*.com
*.exe
*.COM
*.EXE
*.zip
*.dsk
*.DSK
*.woz
*.po
*.do
*.img

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
